WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:04.170
A new villain enters the picture in "Mission:
Impossible — Dead Reckoning Part One."

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:07.630
While he has his merits, we can't help but
long for the return of the bad guy who made

00:00:07.630 --> 00:00:10.259
such a huge impact in the previous film.

00:00:10.259 --> 00:00:13.090
Warning: Spoilers for "Dead Reckoning Part
One" ahead!

00:00:13.090 --> 00:00:17.150
In a franchise fueled on secrets and high-tech
surprises that make the mission all that much

00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:21.109
more difficult, "Dead Reckoning Part One"
distinctly lacked when it came to the shock

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:22.109
factor.

00:00:22.109 --> 00:00:25.240
Sure, there were a few twists here and there,
and jaws dropped seeing Tom Cruise riding

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.460
a dirtbike and ditching it mid-flight, but
it lacked something that the previous movie,

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.090
"Fallout," had: a perfect opposing force against
Ethan Hunt.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:37.290
Henry Cavill's August Walker elevates "Fallout"
to some of the highest highs of the "Mission:

00:00:37.290 --> 00:00:38.320
Impossible" franchise.

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:42.160
He's the hammer to Hunt's scalpel, and their
final showdown on the side of a Himalayan

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.280
mountain is an epic one that demonstrates
Cavill could be just as magnetic trying to

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.210
end the world as he was trying to save it
in other roles.

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:50.210
"This proves nothing.

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:51.950
I'm playing a role.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:52.950
Just like you are."

00:00:52.950 --> 00:00:56.560
Esai Morales' Gabriel slides into the lead
villain role in "Dead Reckoning: Part One,"

00:00:56.560 --> 00:00:59.000
and he provides a different kind of threat.

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:04.049
He's a smoother operator, and frankly, pales
in comparison to Cavill's hulking but equally

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:05.540
manipulative mastermind.

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:10.250
The revelation that Cavill's fist-reloading
CIA man was the brains behind Ethan's problems

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:14.610
made August Walker more of a force to be reckoned
with than Gabriel could ever be.

00:01:14.610 --> 00:01:19.220
Morales' Gabriel gains an edge thanks to a
powerful AI called The Entity, but it actually

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:20.970
makes him a less compelling foe.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.000
As the messenger for the Entity, Morales'
antagonist almost feels like the "Mission:

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.720
Impossible" answer to The Architect from "The
Matrix."

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:31.820
He's a jargon-spouting man of mystery that
doesn't really feel like much of an imposing

00:01:31.820 --> 00:01:32.820
figure.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.080
Also, while Gabriel is supposed to have a
history with Hunt, it doesn't really feel

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.080
like it.

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.650
Everything has to be filled in with flashbacks,
referring to characters who have never been

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:41.860
mentioned before.

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:45.150
That's where Walker making a comeback would
feel so much more impactful.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.009
We've seen these two go toe-to-toe.

00:01:47.009 --> 00:01:51.000
We know they can push each other's buttons,
and seeing more of that would make any future

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:53.579
"Mission: Impossible" chapter with Cavill
all the more enjoyable.

00:01:53.579 --> 00:01:58.110
It'd be the perfect time to have him pay a
return visit as well, given his current schedule.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:01.100
"You're not getting rid of me that easily,
Hunt."

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:05.010
After hanging up the cape as Superman and
passing the White Wolf onto Liam Hemsworth

00:02:05.010 --> 00:02:08.780
for "The Witcher," seeing him strut back on
the scene for "Mission: Impossible", twice

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:11.590
as angry and just as unhinged, would be welcome.

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:15.379
More importantly, it could cement Cavill as
one of the most consequential villains in

00:02:15.379 --> 00:02:16.440
the "Mission: Impossible" franchise.

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:19.490
He'd be a Blofeld to Ethan Hunt's Bond, if
you will.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:23.850
As the world waits with bated breath for a
new James Bond to hit the big screen, Ethan

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:27.890
Hunt and his ensemble of spies have the espionage
action market covered at the moment.

00:02:27.890 --> 00:02:32.030
Calling upon Henry Cavill could establish
August Walker as a permanent threat to Hunt,

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:34.080
just as Blofeld has long been for Bond.

00:02:34.080 --> 00:02:38.209
Much like the lunatic with the top SPECTRE
spot, Walker has already shown his managerial

00:02:38.209 --> 00:02:41.250
skills by handling The Apostles while hiding
in plain sight.

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:45.100
If he managed to go that long without being
detected, it wouldn't be that much of a shock

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:48.950
to see him make a killer comeback as an even
more maniacal force.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:52.569
There is, of course, the matter of Walker
having died by falling off that mountain in

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:56.330
"Fallout," but bringing him back from the
dead wouldn't be such a wild idea.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:03:00.460
Longtime Tom Cruise collaborator Christopher
McQuarrie, who directed the last three entries

00:03:00.460 --> 00:03:03.659
in the "Mission: Impossible" franchise, told
The Hollywood Reporter in 2021,

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:07.830
"I'm in the process of rewriting 'Mission
8' right now, this afternoon I could turn

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:10.340
a page and any actor from the past could come
back.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:13.480
There is no such thing as death in movies,
only unavailability."

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:16.970
What better way to throw Hunt off balance
than setting up a rematch we'd all be hyped

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:17.970
to see?

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:21.530
The stunts in "Dead Reckoning: Part One" are
great, but they'd have been even better under

00:03:21.530 --> 00:03:24.500
the looming shadow of a former foe with thunderous
fists.

